WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
People think we buy houses.

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:11.000
That it's all numbers, contracts, closings,
commissions.

3
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:12.000
We don't.

4
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Well, not really.

5
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.000
What we buy is time for people who've run
out of it.

6
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.000
Every morning starts the same way.

7
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.000
The list is already waiting.

8
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:29.000
And somewhere on that list is a family that
thinks nobody's coming.

9
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:33.000
We go.

10
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:38.000
Last year, foreclosure came for more than
300,000 families.

11
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Most of them never listed, never got the
sign in the yard, the open house, the offers.

12
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.000
No agent.

13
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:47.000
No plan.

14
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.000
Just a clock running down.

15
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:54.000
By the time the letters turn certified, most
folks stop opening the mail.

16
00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.000
Shame does that.

17
00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:58.000
Fear does that.

18
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:05.000
They just needed someone to show up.

19
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:09.000
Solve the problem, and the profit follows.
Every time.

20
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:13.000
Somewhere out there, a family's running out
of options.

21
00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:20.000
Today, we will be the option that matters.

22
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:21.000
Hi, I'm Andrea.

23
00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:25.000
Your virtual onboarding specialist with the
BMH Group.

24
00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:29.577
Thank you for being here. The fact that you
are watching this means you have made a

25
00:01:29.577 --> 00:01:32.000
decision to do something that matters.

26
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:33.000
Not just a job.

27
00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:35.000
Not just a role.

28
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:39.000
Something that genuinely changes people's
lives.

29
00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:42.000
We are glad you are with us at BMH Group.

30
00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:43.000
And we mean that.

31
00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:48.000
Before we get into the training, we want you
to understand something important.

32
00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:53.000
The people you are going to be talking to
are not just names in a CRM.

33
00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:57.000
They are real people carrying real burdens.

34
00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:01.705
And the way you show up for them matters more
than any script or technique we could ever

35
00:02:01.705 --> 00:02:03.000
teach you.

36
00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:07.610
The work you are stepping into is not what
most people picture when they think about

37
00:02:07.610 --> 00:02:09.000
real estate.

38
00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:12.000
You are not going to be showing homes.

39
00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:16.610
You are not going to be negotiating on
behalf of buyers who have options and time on

40
00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:18.000
their side.

41
00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:22.681
You are going to be talking to families in
the middle of some of the hardest moments of

42
00:02:22.681 --> 00:02:24.000
their lives.

43
00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.000
A foreclosure.

44
00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:27.000
A loss.

45
00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:30.000
A property that became too much to carry.

46
00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:34.562
A situation they have been trying to figure
out for months with no clear answer in

47
00:02:34.562 --> 00:02:36.000
sight.

48
00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:40.000
And you are going to help them find a way
through it.

49
00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:41.000
How?

50
00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:44.000
The BMH Group buys houses for cash.

51
00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:45.000
As is.

52
00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:50.579
So a homeowner who needs speed and certainty
can move on without repairs, agents, or

53
00:02:50.579 --> 00:02:53.000
months of waiting.

54
00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:54.000
That's the tool.

55
00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:56.000
This training is about how you use it.

56
00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:58.000
That is fulfilling work.

57
00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:00.000
Real work.

58
00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:05.000
The kind that stays with you long after the
call ends and long after the deal closes.

59
00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:08.000
There is a lot you will learn in this
training.

60
00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.000
The ideal prospect.

61
00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:11.000
The offer.

62
00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:12.000
The process.

63
00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:14.000
The objections.

64
00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:17.000
How to qualify a seller.

65
00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:20.000
How to present a cash offer.

66
00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:24.000
How to handle the moments when a
conversation gets hard.

67
00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:26.000
You will also have a script.

68
00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:28.000
And that script is a valuable tool.

69
00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:34.000
It gives you structure, confidence, and a
clear path through every conversation.

70
00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:40.000
But here is the truth about what actually
makes someone exceptional at this work.

71
00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:43.000
It is not the script. The script tells you
what to say.

72
00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:48.000
But the best reps know when to put the
script down and just listen.

73
00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:50.000
When to slow down.

74
00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:56.000
When to ask one more question instead of
moving to the next line.

75
00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:01.244
The most powerful thing you can develop is
the ability to lead a homeowner to the best

76
00:04:01.244 --> 00:04:04.000
possible path for their situation.

77
00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:05.000
Not our path.

78
00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:08.000
Maybe not our company. Their path.

79
00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:12.978
When you sit in a conversation with a distressed
seller and you are genuinely focused on

80
00:04:12.978 --> 00:04:17.000
understanding what they need and not just
pushing them toward a yes.

81
00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:19.000
Something shifts.

82
00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:20.000
They feel it.

83
00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:21.000
They trust you.

84
00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:26.000
And trust is what moves a deal forward more
than anything else ever will.

85
00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:31.000
The best closers at BMH Group are not the
ones who follow the script perfectly.

86
00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:35.730
They are the ones who know when to set it
down and just be present with the person on

87
00:04:35.730 --> 00:04:40.268
the other end of the phone. In the training
ahead, you will learn exactly who our

88
00:04:40.268 --> 00:04:44.615
sellers are, what we offer them, how our
process works, and how to handle the

89
00:04:44.615 --> 00:04:47.000
conversations that feel the hardest.

90
00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:50.000
But carry this with you through every
module.

91
00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:52.000
You are not here to sell.

92
00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:56.000
You are here to consult and provide options.

93
00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:57.000
Never pushy.

94
00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:59.000
Never desperate.

95
00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:04.053
You are here to help families overcome
difficult situations and walk away with clarity,

96
00:05:04.053 --> 00:05:07.000
certainty, and the ability to move forward.

97
00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:08.000
That is the mission.

98
00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:12.000
Everything else is just the skill set that
makes you better at it.

99
00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:15.000
Welcome, and we are glad you are on board.

100
00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:18.000
Now let's get to work. Your training starts
now.
